  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 204 PM MDT SUN OCT 4 2026\nThe upper-level ridging over the area will continue through \nThursday, with highs 10 to 20 degrees above normal. This pattern\nwill support mostly clear skies and light winds. On Friday, an \nupper level trough will approach the Pacific Northwest. This \nsystem will start impacting the area first by increasing winds \nover the higher terrain Friday afternoon, with gusts 20 to 30 \nmph expected. Temperatures will remain warm Friday afternoon \nahead of a cold front moving NW to SE across the area starting \nearly Saturday. This cold front will cool temperatures by about \n15 degrees when comparing Friday afternoon high temperatures to \nSaturday. Confidence on the evolution of the trough decreases by\nSunday, but additional cooling is likely as the trough moves \noverhead at some point during the weekend. Precipitation chances\nlook to be highest in the high terrain of SW Idaho (20-40% \nchance) Saturday and Sunday with a 10-20% chance elsewhere. \nWinds will also remain breezy over the weekend.",
